<p>Why this page exists, in the project's own words: a signature on a tower this tall can only be a review or a rubber stamp, and the difference between them is the whole of whether the panel/author separation the method is built on still holds. That review is no longer on the docket — at <strong>Session 4k it occurred</strong>: the author ruled item-by-item and closed the build. But closing it tested nothing against the world (by the project's own C-017, nothing can be in this setup), the drain's one fire was author-initiated — the self-initiated "of its own motion" channel stands at zero across four readings — and the author's concession records that no genuinely foreign reader, grader, or forker will arrive here; his judgment stands as the terminal ratifier. The tower is <strong>resolved by one human check, not validated by any outside one</strong>. The plurality is set down, not earned back.</p>

<p class="companion-note">Read this beside the <a href="{{ '/diagrams/' | url }}">self-audit &amp; figures</a> page: that one counts what the project made; this one says how much of it a person has confirmed.</p>
